The Skills are adapted for k-Coder's ExtensionService, workspace policy,
bounded tools, and local-only persistence. Upstream executable helpers,
credential files, and unavailable runtime integrations are not bundled.

Single documented exception:

  robot-pack/webapp-testing/scripts/with_server.py

is not upstream code. It is a local k-Coder implementation written for this
repository (standard library only, no third-party or copied sources) that starts
short-lived local development servers, waits for them to answer, runs one
verification command, and then stops the servers and their process trees.

The host never executes it. It is a read-only Skill resource: the model may only
obtain it through `skill_resource_read` and run it through `run_command`, where
policy assessment, sandbox rules, command timeouts, approvals, and audit still
apply. It installs nothing and contacts no remote host. Any other Python or
Playwright dependency is a user-provided prerequisite and is not bundled.
